WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.492
The next day Ally and Flo were working the lunch shift.

2
00:00:05.493 --> 00:00:09.289
The day had been busy, but things were finally slowing down.

3
00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:13.327
Flo was in the kitchen with Melanie and Ray.

4
00:00:13.328 --> 00:00:18.380
"At last," Ally said. "I can check my phone."

5
00:00:18.381 --> 00:00:22.066
But the message she'd been waiting for wasn't there.

6
00:00:22.067 --> 00:00:26.409
"Why hasn't Lainie's assistant called me back yet?" she mumbled.

7
00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:28.698
"The eclipse is coming up!"

8
00:00:28.699 --> 00:00:32.714
"Did you say 'eclipse'?" Tina had walked into the diner.

9
00:00:32.715 --> 00:00:35.130
"I love eclipses!"

10
00:00:35.131 --> 00:00:40.960
"Oh, hi, Tina. Your pickup order will be ready soon," Ally said.

11
00:00:40.961 --> 00:00:44.379
"Thanks." Tina sat at the counter to wait.

12
00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:48.801
"I love my new job so much, I don't mind picking up lunch for everyone.

13
00:00:48.802 --> 00:00:51.536
I'm hoping to move up the ranks quickly, so—"

14
00:00:51.537 --> 00:00:55.401
Ally's phone rang. It was Lainie's assistant.

15
00:00:55.402 --> 00:01:00.922
"Excuse me." Ally hurried off to take the call. "Hello?"

16
00:01:00.923 --> 00:01:03.719
"Hi, Ally," the assistant said.

17
00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:07.871
"Lainie would love to have you visit and see her research.

18
00:01:07.872 --> 00:01:13.003
We'll send a car for you in two days to take you to one of Lainie's private jets."

19
00:01:13.004 --> 00:01:17.408
"Yay!" Ally squealed. "Thank you!"

20
00:01:17.409 --> 00:01:19.820
She hung up and did a happy dance.

21
00:01:19.821 --> 00:01:23.236
"Good news?" Tina asked.

22
00:01:23.237 --> 00:01:25.966
"The best!" Ally cheered.

23
00:01:25.967 --> 00:01:30.422
"I'm going to get my pow— I'm going to Patagonia!"

24
00:01:30.423 --> 00:01:35.372
"How fun! But why there?" Tina asked.

25
00:01:35.373 --> 00:01:40.816
"The solar eclipse will be visible there, and I want to view it," Ally said.

26
00:01:40.817 --> 00:01:43.234
"You're so lucky!" Tina said.

27
00:01:43.235 --> 00:01:49.969
"Have you heard of Dr. Lloyd? He's one reason I wanted to work at the museum.

28
00:01:49.970 --> 00:01:58.038
Anyway, he has a theory that eclipses are a way to attract aliens to Earth."

29
00:01:58.039 --> 00:02:01.907
Ally gulped. "He does?"

30
00:02:01.908 --> 00:02:05.222
Tina nodded. "I hope it's true.

31
00:02:05.223 --> 00:02:10.301
I'm determined to see a real alien for myself one day."

32
00:02:10.302 --> 00:02:12.874
"Uh, well, good luck with that!"

33
00:02:12.875 --> 00:02:19.033
Ally got busy and tried to avoid eye contact with Tina until her order was ready.

34
00:02:19.034 --> 00:02:24.970
"Thanks for the interesting conversation, Ally," Tina called as she left the diner.

35
00:02:24.971 --> 00:02:28.482
"What did she mean by 'interesting'?" Ally thought.

36
00:02:28.483 --> 00:02:37.255
"I wish I could read her mind. But I'll have my powers back soon enough!"

37
00:02:37.256 --> 00:02:40.641
Ally was in her room when her phone rang again.

38
00:02:40.642 --> 00:02:43.567
"Hi, Ally," Lainie's assistant said.

39
00:02:43.568 --> 00:02:47.703
"I forgot to remind you, don't forget to pack your passport. Bye!"

40
00:02:47.704 --> 00:02:49.759
Ally smacked her forehead.

41
00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:53.077
"I forgot all about that!

42
00:02:53.078 --> 00:02:56.949
Alpha, please research getting a passport."

43
00:02:56.950 --> 00:03:03.431
"A passport is the document that humans need to travel out of their home country," Alpha said.

44
00:03:03.432 --> 00:03:07.121
"I know. But how do I get one?" Ally asked.

45
00:03:07.122 --> 00:03:12.535
Alpha blinked. "One, a photograph with your likeness must be taken.

46
00:03:12.536 --> 00:03:15.871
Two, an application must be filled out.

47
00:03:15.872 --> 00:03:20.483
Three, you must pay a fee."

48
00:03:20.484 --> 00:03:24.135
"Ugh!" Ally's hopes crumbled.

49
00:03:24.136 --> 00:03:35.258
"Why does everything cost money on this planet?" she moaned as Mateo knocked on her door.

50
00:03:35.259 --> 00:03:38.574
"I thought I heard you come home," Mateo said.

51
00:03:38.575 --> 00:03:43.620
"I haven't had any luck yet finding UserPFM5, but I'm getting closer.

52
00:03:43.621 --> 00:03:46.650
I think the person lives near the park.

53
00:03:46.651 --> 00:03:49.945
I was wondering if Alpha could help me now."

54
00:03:49.946 --> 00:03:52.231
"Sure," Ally said.

55
00:03:52.232 --> 00:03:57.807
"As soon as she figures out how I can get a passport. Fast!"

56
00:03:57.808 --> 00:04:01.038
"You heard from Lainie?" Mateo asked.

57
00:04:01.039 --> 00:04:04.233
"Yes! She's sending a car and a plane for me.

58
00:04:04.234 --> 00:04:07.113
But I have to get a passport first."

59
00:04:07.114 --> 00:04:11.885
"Applications for a passport require proof of birth," Alpha said.

60
00:04:11.886 --> 00:04:17.806
"I'm alive!" Ally said. "How much more proof do they need?"

61
00:04:17.807 --> 00:04:19.530
"Incorrect, Allyzooba.

62
00:04:19.531 --> 00:04:22.584
Proof that you were born in a country on Earth."

63
00:04:22.585 --> 00:04:27.020
"But I don't have that!" Ally wailed.

64
00:04:27.021 --> 00:04:31.620
"Alpha, can you search for a different solution?" Mateo asked.

65
00:04:31.621 --> 00:04:34.564
"Affirmative."

66
00:04:34.565 --> 00:04:45.314
While Alpha went back to work, Ally told Mateo about her conversation with Tina, Melanie's shake, and her comment about Ally's meld medallion.

67
00:04:45.315 --> 00:04:49.238
"Lots of people notice your medallion," Mateo said.

68
00:04:49.239 --> 00:04:53.485
"And you always think it means they know the truth about you.

69
00:04:53.486 --> 00:04:56.664
Remember when you first met Lainie?

70
00:04:56.665 --> 00:04:59.607
You were sure she knew your secret.

71
00:04:59.608 --> 00:05:06.213
Besides, you don't even have your powers now, so why would anyone suspect you?"

72
00:05:06.214 --> 00:05:08.130
"You're right," Ally said.

73
00:05:08.131 --> 00:05:12.795
"I was suspicious of Barry when I first met him, and now I think he's great.

74
00:05:12.796 --> 00:05:18.481
I guess it's not very Astralian of me to be suspicious all the time."

75
00:05:18.482 --> 00:05:23.232
"Your powers are not what make you Astralian, Allyzooba," Alpha said.

76
00:05:23.233 --> 00:05:26.013
"But your duty to be helpful does.

77
00:05:26.014 --> 00:05:31.953
And even from inside this inferior technology, it is my duty to aid you in your mission."

78
00:05:31.954 --> 00:05:36.376
"Did you find a way to get me a passport?" Ally asked hopefully.

79
00:05:36.377 --> 00:05:45.987
"Negative," Alpha said. "But I did locate the address of UserPFM5."

